---
/** The Operator's console as a page (also the control room's console). The island needs JS; this page says what it is without it. */
import Shell from '@/layouts/Shell.astro';
import Operator from '@/islands/Operator';
import '@/styles/operator.css';
---

<Shell
  title="Operator"
  description="The Operator: an on-device agent that retrieves from Kevil Patel's fact ledger, cites its sources, proposes actions you confirm, and declines when the lab has no evidence."
  path="/operator/"
>
  <section class="wrap operator">
    <p class="eyebrow">Control room · Operator console</p>
    <h1>Ask the lab. It cites or declines.</h1>
    <p class="operator__lead">
      The Operator runs entirely in your browser: lexical and semantic retrieval over the fact ledger, a
      job-description matcher, and validated tools that move the floor only when you click. An optional
      on-device language model can be downloaded for grounded prose; its size is shown first and nothing
      downloads on its own.
    </p>
    <Operator client:load />
    <noscript>
      <p class="as-stated">
        The console needs JavaScript. Without it, the <a href="/resume/">résumé</a>, the{' '}
        <a href="/work/">case studies</a> and the <a href="/machines/telemetry-refinery/">machine pages</a>{' '}
        carry every fact with its source.
      </p>
    </noscript>
    <p class="as-stated">
      Trust instruments: groundedness = cited sentences ÷ sentences · evidence coverage = cited chunks ÷
      retrieved · refusals = answers declined for lack of evidence. Formulas are published in{' '}
      <a href="/generated/ai-manifest.json">ai-manifest.json</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Shell>

<style>
  @layer components {
    .operator {
      padding-block: var(--space-7);
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-4);
    }
    .operator__lead {
      font-size: var(--text-lg);
      color: var(--ink-2);
    }
  }
</style>
